****

Perhaps the most studied line of the infrared calcium triplet, consisting of 8498, 8542 and 8662. 8498 has fainter prominences and features in general, 
while 8662 is a bit blended with a Paschen hydrogen at 8665 (n=13), and 8542 with 8545.3 (n=15). 

The rendered Ca II 8542 disk looks like an anemic version of Calcium II K, somewhat brighter disk compared to the plages, bright plages surrounded by a bit darker halo on the disk, with less contrast in filaments and prominences. 
